Original commit body from 9531d6c6e384ddafb904f01385d8108fcb80acb3:

One edge per (src, dst, edge_type) is the right call-graph model and is
unchanged -- emitting one edge per call site would multiply the graph (a
single Go function's fmt.Printf calls alone turn 1 edge into 12, inflating
every centrality and fan-out metric downstream). What was wrong is that
edge.line -- whichever site happened to be encountered FIRST -- was the only
site any consumer could recover.

ADR-0017 section 4 cannot work without the rest: deciding what a dataflow use
at line U flows into requires knowing which callee is invoked at line U, and
with one line per relationship that question was unanswerable for every call
site but one. This is the sixth prerequisite of WI-kabif, absent from its
filed list of four.

The survivor now carries the sorted union of collapsed sites, its own line
included -- so a consumer never has to remember to union edge.line, which is
a silent single-site regression waiting to happen. A single-site edge carries
NO call_lines key: absence is the contract for "exactly one site, and it is
line", and a one-element list on every edge would add a list to every edge of
every behavior map while saying nothing line does not already say.

Both collapse sites, not just the obvious one. apply_external_id_remap runs
AFTER deduplicate_edges and collapses again -- two edges genuinely distinct at
dedup time (distinct external dsts) become one once both dsts remap to a single
boundary node. It unions call_lines the way it already unions referring_paths.

Capped at 50 (sibling of _REFERRING_PATHS_CAP), because generated code can call
one target hundreds of times from one function. Truncation keeps the lowest N
and is conservative for every consumer: knowing fewer call sites can only
narrow what a dataflow walk adjudicates, never broaden it.

Measured on hypergumbo's own repo and verified in both directions rather than
counted: 13,121 of 141,312 edges (9.29%) record more than one site -- median 2,
p95 7, 28 at the cap -- adding 0.22% to the artifact (411 KB of 186 MB). Every
line recorded for catalog.py:file -> _ts is a genuine _ts(...) call site, and
the UNRECORDED lines inside the same caller's span (cli.py:2559-2568) contain
no .get( -- so the field records call sites, not "every line in the caller".

Registered in axis_meta_keys (the Edge.meta vocabulary registry) and
regenerated into docs/schema.json; a meta key producers write and consumers
read without a registry entry is the drift that registry exists to police.

